"defenceVal":"1","hp":"140","price":"500","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"father":{"label":{"zh":"父亲","en":"Father"},"people":[{"id":"WJ10315","code":"0"}]},"family":{"label":{"zh":"亲属","en":"Relatives"},"people":[{"id":"WJ10110","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI106115","name":{"zh":"陇西辛氏","en":"The Xin clan of Longxi"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"出自姒姓，夏朝开国君主启封庶子于莘（今陕西合阳），后因音近改莘为辛，遂以辛为氏。其先祖本居陇西，东汉建武年间东迁至颍川阳翟（今河南禹州）。西汉时期，辛庆忌以功封营平侯，其子孙因受吕宽案牵连被诛杀，导致家族在东汉近二百年间沉寂无闻，直到三国时期才再度崛起。辛评、辛毗兄弟先仕袁绍，官渡之战后辛毗归曹，为曹操出谋划策，官至卫尉、侍中，封颍乡侯，位列九卿。其女辛宪英以才智闻名，预言钟会叛乱的结局。","en":"Originating from the Si surname, Qi, the founding Ruler of the Xia dynasty, enfeoffed his concubine-born son at Shen (modern-day Heyang, Shaanxi), which later evolved phonetically into Xin, becoming their clan name. Their ancestors originally resided in Longxi and migrated East to Yangzhai in Yingchuan (modern-day Yuzhou, Henan) during the Jianwu era of the Eastern Han. During the Western Han, Xin Qingji was enfeoffed as the Marquis of Yingping for his merit, but his descendants were executed due to implication in the Lu Kuan affair, leaving the clan in obscurity for nearly two hundred years throughout the Eastern Han until their resurgence in the Three Kingdoms period. The brothers Xin Ping and Xin Pi initially served Yuan Shao, after the Battle of Guandu, Xin Pi joined Cao Cao and served as a key strategist, rising to Commandant of the Guards and Attendant Palace Gentleman, enfeoffed as Marquis of Yingxiang and ranking among the Nine Ministers. His daughter Xin Xianying was famed for her wisdom, accurately predicting the outcome of Zhong Hui's rebellion."},"talent":{"military":"1","commerce":"5","politics":"7"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":null,"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},